{"id":"chatcmpl-14b2eba8-808c-49ca-b4d0-8a4e55696a39","object":"chat.completion","created":1795246782,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task succeeds by first establishing image orientation and view type before committing to a laterality-dependent answer, then using a domain expert tool to resolve ambiguity that standard reporting tools cannot handle. The key insight is that laterality on lateral views is non-obvious and requires targeted expert reasoning about anatomical landmarks rather than default frontal-view assumptions.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When the answer hinges on spatial laterality (left vs right), first verify image orientation/view type via metadata or reporting tools before interpreting the finding.\",\n    \"Use a specialized expert tool with a targeted, anatomy-specific question when a general reporting tool returns not-applicable or insufficient detail.\",\n    \"Treat 'not_applicable' or null outputs from a tool as informative signals about view type or data limitations, not as failures.\",\n    \"Escalate to a second, more specific expert query that names the discriminating anatomical landmarks (e.g., posterior location, spine overlap, diaphragm contour) when the first pass leaves laterality unresolved.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Confirm view type and orientation markers early; laterality rules differ between frontal and lateral views, so never assume standard left/right assignment.\",\n    \"Tool-orchestrated reasoning\": \"Chain a general reporting tool to establish context, then a specialized expert tool with a narrowly scoped question to resolve the specific ambiguity.\",\n    \"Ambiguity resolution\": \"When a finding could map to multiple options differing only by a spatial attribute, isolate that attribute and query specifically for its discriminating landmarks.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm image view type and orientation markers before assigning left/right laterality.\",\n    \"Verify the final answer's spatial claim (posterior location, side) against explicit anatomical landmarks cited by the expert tool.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":550,"total_tokens":925,"completion_tokens":375,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":550},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":375}}}